# Sovereign Voice Pipeline — LOCKDOWN

The Gemini Native Audio voice pipeline is FROZEN infrastructure. It works. Do not touch it.

## Protected Files — READ ONLY

- `server/geminiVoice.ts` — browser `/ws/gemini-live` proxy
- `server/voiceStream.ts` — Twilio Media Stream → Gemini bridge
- `server/voiceGemini.ts` — audio WebSocket orchestration
- `server/voiceSession.ts` — session state management
- `server/audioCodec.ts` — 16-bit PCM encode/decode
- `server/config/geminiLiveProtocol.ts` — FINICKY. One wrong change breaks voice entirely.
- `server/config/geminiSystemInstructions.ts`
- `server/config/geminiToolDeclarations.ts`
- `client/src/services/voice/**`
- `client/public/clear-voice-processor.js` — AudioWorklet. Do not move or rename.

## Absolute Prohibitions

- NEVER hardcode `GEMINI_MODEL_ID` or any model string. Model is set in Doppler only.
- NEVER modify audio sample rates. Input: 16kHz. Output: 24kHz. These are hardware specs.
- NEVER add a new AI provider to the voice pipeline. Gemini is the sole voice engine.
- NEVER change the `/ws/gemini-live` or `/ws/voice-stream` route paths.
- NEVER modify WebSocket handshake logic without an explicit voice test task.

## If You Think You Need to Change This

You don't. If a bug is confirmed, open a voice-specific task. Do not fix the voice pipeline as a side effect of another task.
